WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:07.120
Hey Thoughty2 here. Twitter was started in
2006 by four internet entrepreneurs, and it

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:14.630
took 3 years to get to one billion tweets.
However, today over one billion tweets are

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:23.619
sent every week. Here's some really interesting
things you probably don't know about Twitter.

00:00:23.619 --> 00:00:32.189
1. Twitter was actually created on a playground.
The founding team members were at the top

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:38.410
of a slide in a playground in San Francisco,
when Jack Dorsey said "I've got an idea so

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:42.949
simple that you don't even think about it
- you just write."

00:00:42.949 --> 00:00:50.000
2. At first glance it may seem that, unlike
most websites, Twitter is advertisement free.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.559
But that's not quite true, Twitter is a business,
and it does make money through cleverly disguised

00:00:55.559 --> 00:01:02.489
advertisements. Twitter has two main revenue
streams, firstly Google and Bing pay Twitter

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:08.610
a handsome license fee so that they can include
tweets in their realtime search results. And

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:15.750
secondly big brands such as Starbucks, Coca-Cola,
Red Bull and many others pay Twitter for sponsored

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:22.640
tweets which appear in Twitter search results.
Brands can also pay for "promoted trends"

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.531
which appear amongst the other naturally trending
topics. The cost for a Promoted Trend in the

00:01:28.531 --> 00:01:32.840
United States for one day is $200,000.

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:40.399
3. Twitter gave the city of Boston a promoted
trend free of charge after the Boston Marathon

00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:45.310
bombing in April 2013. The trend was #OneBoston.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:52.290
4. But when it comes to profit, Twitter is
very different the likes of Facebook, Google

00:01:52.290 --> 00:02:00.729
and Apple. Because Twitter has never made
a single dime of profit. In 2014 Twitter made

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:10.229
a net loss of $578 million. Which can be attributed
to its rapid expansion and excruciatingly

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.010
high operating costs.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:18.890
5. But why are Twitter's operating costs so
high. Well, it has a lot to do with the fact

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:27.220
that 500 million tweets are sent every day.
Which is an astonishing 6,000 tweets per second.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:32.230
All those messages take an awful lot of processing
power and storage.

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:37.840
6. A single day's worth of Twitter posts would
fill a 10 million page book.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:45.580
7. The person with the most followers on Twitter
is Katy Perry who has 68 million followers.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:48.970
Second is Justin Bieber and third is Barack
Obama.

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:55.190
8. The most followed brand on Twitter is YouTube,
which has 50 million followers.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:01.890
9. Twitter wasn't always called Twitter, and
it didn't always have a bird as a mascot.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:08.879
When it launched it was called Twttr and it
looked like this. When it was being created

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:13.099
"Friendstalker" was also considered as a potential
name.

00:03:13.099 --> 00:03:20.090
10. Twitter later added it's famous blue bird
as its mascot, who by the way is called Larry.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:23.240
Named after basketball player, Larry Bird.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:29.159
11. Twitter is responsible for starting the
hashtag phenomenon. The first ever use of

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:36.700
the hashtag on Twitter was, #barcamp, posted
by an open source software advocate Chris

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:43.709
Messina. Who thought it would be a good idea
to use the hashtag to signify a group. Chris

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:51.220
was inspired by the hashtag's heavy use in
IRC chatrooms. He is now referred to as "The

00:03:51.220 --> 00:03:52.220
Hashtag Godfather".

00:03:52.220 --> 00:04:01.800
12. We've all heard of a hashtag, but how
about a cashtag? Cashtags are used on Twitter

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.890
by Wall Street tweeters interested in tracking
the news around stocks.

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:13.520
13. Speaking of news, Twitter has become the
de-facto source for global news. When something

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:20.480
big happens around the world news of it spreads
on Twitter via hashtags faster than any other

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:26.270
news source in the world. Because of this
Twitter is now the primary resource for the

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.020
majority of TV news stations.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:36.421
14. Twitter is seen as the home of super fast,
and often instantaneous communication. So

00:04:36.421 --> 00:04:44.130
it may come as a surprise that between 2008
and 2010 to help keep the site online Twitter

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:51.470
had a "guy with a pager". The pager would
rotate between four people who would constantly

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:57.220
monitor Twitter to check if it went offline.
These days they're a bit more high tech and

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:01.130
use automated monitoring systems to keep the
website online.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:09.010
15. Twitter has 288 million active monthly
users. 80% of whom access the service through

00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:10.530
mobile devices.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:16.970
16. In the early days of Twitter, they were
thinking about introducing a "worship" button.

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:22.510
If you worshipped someone, you would get every
single one of their messages, but the idea

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:23.920
was ditched.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:31.210
17. Twitter CEO Dick Costolo said any Twitter
employee can launch any test to 1 percent

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:34.660
of users without any senior approvals.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:42.160
18. The most retweeted tweet ever was by Ellen
DeGeneres with her star-studded selfie tweet

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:48.020
at the 2014 Oscars. It got 3.4 million retweets.

00:05:48.020 --> 00:05:53.660
19. Tweets containing hashtags receive two
times the levels of engagement than those

00:05:53.660 --> 00:06:00.440
without hashtags, yet only 24 percent of tweets
actually contain hashtags.

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:07.710
20. Twitter is on Twitter, but Twitter is
also on Facebook, and Facebook is also on

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:13.650
Twitter. Twitter is also on YouTube and YouTube
is on Twitter.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:21.610
21. There is a Twitter account called everyword
that has manually tweeted every single word

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:26.800
in the English dictionary. The task took them
7 years to complete.

00:06:26.800 --> 00:06:33.550
22. There is also Twitter account with the
username SignOut that has only ever tweeted

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:42.100
once but has 1,435 followers. Why? Because,
apparently some Twitter users think that they

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:45.840
can sign out of Twitter by following the account.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:53.080
23. Visiting either Twittter.com (with an
extra t) or Twiter.com (missing a t) will

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:56.210
both redirect you to the official website.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:01.850
24. The average number of followers of all
users on Twitter is 208.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:06.770
25. The FBI has a dictionary of Twitter slang.

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:14.120
26. In order to promote diversity the official
twitter account of Sweden is given to a new

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:17.460
random citizen every week to manage.

00:07:17.460 --> 00:07:25.380
27. The Library of Congress is archiving every
single tweet sent by an American citizen,

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:31.190
because they believe each tweet is an important
part of the national narrative of American

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:38.380
history. Their database of tweets is over
150 terabytes and growing.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:44.500
28. The CIA also reads up to 5 million tweets
a day. They could be reading yours right now.

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.940
29. 44% of Twitter users have never sent a
single Tweet. They just use the site for stalk

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:49.940
people.

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:55.480
30. A report found that over 50% of Justin
Bieber's Twitter followers are fake.

00:07:55.480 --> 00:08:01.870
31. According to the Vatican, you can reduce
the time you spend in purgatory by following

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:04.580
the Pope on Twitter. That sounds legit.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:12.580
32. And finally, Twitter may not yet be making
a profit but it is worth $31 billion and is

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:16.150
the 8th most visited website on the internet.
And financial analysts predict that Twitter

00:08:16.150 --> 00:08:17.150
could finally become profitable by the end
of 2015, so don't give up on the old bird

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:19.330
just yet.
Thanks for the view, subscribe for more Thoughty2.

